{"id":"aa318ffe-eaf5-4113-a494-f054c73cd2e9","year":"2026-2027","code":"CFBGR01705","facultyCode":"cf","facultyTitle":{"en":"Campus Fryslân","nl":"Campus Fryslân"},"title":{"en":"Ecosystem Processes and Services (100)","nl":""},"fullTitle":{"en":"Ecosystem Processes & Services (100)","nl":""},"goals":{"en":"Upon the successful completion of this course, students will be able to:\n-\tExplain the importance of ecosystems structure in the biochemical cycles and the correlation between environment and ecosystem functioning. \n-\tDevelop a mental model of how ecosystem spatial and temporal complexity shapes ecosystem functioning. \n-\tEvaluate how ecosystem processes are connected to human wellbeing through the concept of ecosystem services and socio-ecological systems. \n-\tAssess how abrupt change impacts ecosystem processes and services. \n-\tEvaluate how ecosystems have changed and continue to change in the Anthropocene. \n-\tRecognize and reflect on their personal contributions to the outcomes, insights, and behaviours towards their own learning process. \n","nl":""},"description":{"en":"How are ecosystems defined? How are changes in ecosystems monitored and what are the implications of those changes to our wellbeing? \r\n\r\nIn the Ecosystem Processes course we will explore the structure, processes and interactions in the ecosystems. We will identify the indicators used to assess ecosystem integrity and explore the current threats and its implications for the balance of the earth system. During the course, we will analyse the concept of ecosystem services and its applications.","nl":""},"credits":5.00,"hours":4,"levels":["BACHELOR"],"formats":[],"formatsExplanation":{"en":"","nl":""},"assessmentsExplanation":{"en":"","nl":""},"courseTypes":[{"id":"0efe8825-5870-4b94-8080-2303d45bb43f","position":0,"optionList":{"id":"639c4fba-cddd-4593-acb5-5c11b667a363","textEn":"Bachelor","textNl":"Bachelor","position":1,"deletedSince":null,"availableSince":null}}],"prerequisites